clk: qcom: clk-alpha-pll: set the FSM legacy mode of Trion/Lucid PLLs

SUPPORTS_FSM_LEGACY_MODE is only acted on by clk_fabia_pll_configure(),
but gcc-sm6375 marks its Lucid PLLs GPLL8, GPLL10 and GPLL11 with it,
and clk_trion_pll_configure() (clk_lucid_pll_configure()) ignores the
flag. The vendor kernel's Lucid configure sets PLL_FSM_LEGACY_MODE for
it. Without the bit GPLL11 never locks on SM4375 (Xiaomi Redmi Note 12
5G): "gpll11 failed to enable!" when Venus enables its clocks.

Set the bit in the Trion/Lucid configure as the Fabia one does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c
index f8313f9d0..0dbf59067 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c
@@ -1746,6 +1746,10 @@ void clk_trion_pll_configure(struct clk_alpha_pll *pll, struct regmap *regmap,
 	clk_alpha_pll_write_config(regmap, PLL_TEST_CTL_U1(pll),
 					config->test_ctl_hi1_val);
 
+	if (pll->flags & SUPPORTS_FSM_LEGACY_MODE)
+		regmap_update_bits(regmap, PLL_MODE(pll), PLL_FSM_LEGACY_MODE,
+				   PLL_FSM_LEGACY_MODE);
+
 	regmap_update_bits(regmap, PLL_MODE(pll), PLL_UPDATE_BYPASS,
 			   PLL_UPDATE_BYPASS);
 
